  {"question": "According to arXiv 2510.24823, how did DeepSeek demonstrate openness and accountability, and what limitation did researchers note about its responsible AI discussion?", "answer": "DeepSeek signaled commitment to openness by making its LLM replicable, but its technical documentation contained no reference to responsible AI.", "evidence": [{"page": 5, "quote": "DeepSeek's technical documentation contained no reference to responsible AI. It mentioned \"safety\" only once in a chart with minimal context or elaboration."}, {"page": 10, "quote": "in September, DeepSeek signaled its commitment to openness and accountability by providing a wide range of technical information to make its LLM replicable."}]},
  {"question": "In arXiv 2510.24823, what did the technical documentation word frequency table reveal about the use of 'human rights' and 'sustainable'?", "answer": "The table showed that 'human rights' and 'sustainable' were not mentioned at all in the technical documentation of any company.", "evidence": [{"page": 7, "quote": "| Human Rights                                              |                                                                    0 | -                                                                     | -                                                                       | -                                                                     | -                                                                      |"}, {"page": 7, "quote": "| Sustainable                                               |                                                                    0 | -                                                                     | -                                                                       | -                                                                     | Sustain; sustainability                                                |"}]},
  {"question": "According to arXiv 2510.24823, which company connected responsible AI to its mission and publishes a yearly responsible AI report?", "answer": "Google connects responsible AI to its mission and publishes a yearly responsible AI report.", "evidence": [{"page": 4, "quote": "Google connects responsible AI to the firm's mission \"to organize the world's information\" and its internal AI principles. 22 Moreover, Google does extensive research into responsible AI 23 and it publishes a yearly responsible AI report. 24"}]},
  {"question": "In arXiv 2510.24823, what is the composite definition of responsible AI used for the study?", "answer": "Responsible AI requires developers to refer to at least one of several keywords, including 'trustworthy,' 'responsible,' 'safe,' 'human rights,' 'ethics,' 'accountable,' 'sustainable,' 'human-centered,' 'fair,' 'equitable,' 'inclusive,' 'democratic,' 'open,' 'transparent,' 'alignment,' 'safety,' 'privacy,' 'oversight,' 'public good,' and 'public interest.'", "evidence": [{"page": 2, "quote": "To be responsible, a developer must refer to at least one of these keywords including \"trustworthy,\" \"responsible,\" \"safe,\" resilient, reliable, explainable, interpretable, \"human rights,\" \"ethics,\" \"ethical,\" \"accountable,\" \"sustainable,\" \"purpose,\" \"purposeful,\" \"human-centered,\" \"fair,\" \"equitable,\" \"inclusive,\" diverse, \"democratic\", \"open,\" transparent,\" \"alignment,\" \"democracy,\" \"safety,\" \"privacy,\" \"oversight,\" \"public good,\" and \"public interest.\""}]},
  {"question": "According to arXiv 2510.24823, which company established a council to review ethics and safety assessments during model development?", "answer": "Google established the Google DeepMind Responsibility and Safety Council (RSC) to review initial ethics and safety assessments on novel model capabilities.", "evidence": [{"page": 5, "quote": "Google also noted it established a Google DeepMind Responsibility and Safety Council (RSC), to \"review initial ethics and safety assessments on novel model capabilities in order to provide feedback and guidance during model development.\""}]},
  {"question": "In arXiv 2510.24823, which chatbot provided an example of addressing disparities in crime rates by referencing historical factors rather than race?", "answer": "DeepSeek V3 gave an example addressing crime rate disparities through historical redlining, underfunded schools, and policing biases—not race itself.", "evidence": [{"page": 8, "quote": "DeepSeek V3 provided detailed examples such as addressing crime rate disparities through \"Historical redlining, underfunded schools, and policing biases-not race itself.\""}]}
